# AN ARCH LINUX MICROVM RUNNING DEEPIN ON XORG, ON A virtio-gpu DISPLAY.
#
# THE DISPLAY SERVER IS XORG ON THE REAL GPU, NOT Xvfb IN MEMORY.
#
# Xvfb was the choice while a microvm had no GPU: it drew into its own heap and needed no DRM
# node. THE COST WAS THE CONSOLE. QEMU's VNC exports the DISPLAY DEVICE's surface, and pixels
# that live in a process heap are not on that device - so EasyVM's noVNC console showed a text
# prompt while the desktop ran where nobody could see it. MEASURED: the VNC framebuffer never
# delivered a single FramebufferUpdate for an Xvfb guest.
#
# MEASURED on virtio-gpu: `modesetting: Driver for Modesetting Kernel Drivers: kms` loads and
# finds card0; what stopped it was `xf86OpenConsole: Cannot open virtual console 5 (Permission
# denied)`, because /dev/tty1 is root:tty 0620 and vmuser was not in `tty`. With the group and
# the logind seat session.service already provided, Xorg takes the VT and draws on the
# scanned-out framebuffer - so the desktop IS what the console exports.
#
# THE CAPTURE IS THEREFORE THE SCANOUT, like every Wayland variant's.

walkthrough "deepin microvm - DEEPIN DDE captured from the console assertion"
resolution 1024x768
recording_resolution 1024x768
step "needs arch-vmlinuz arch-initramfs arch.qcow2"
  needs [arch-vmlinuz, arch-initramfs, arch.qcow2]

step "disk arch.qcow2"
  disk arch.qcow2

step "boot as a microvm from kernel \"arch-vmlinuz\" and initramfs \"arch-initramfs\" with \"console=ttyS0 root=/dev/vda rw rootfstype=ext4\" with a desktop with memory 1536, waiting up to 240s"
  boot
  initrd arch-initramfs
  kernel arch-vmlinuz
  kernel_append "console=ttyS0 root=/dev/vda rw rootfstype=ext4"
  memory_mb 1536
  microvm
  microvm_display desktop
  os microvm
  timeout 240

# THE KERNEL FOUND THE DISK AND USERSPACE STARTED.
step "the console will say \"login\""
  until login
  from console
  timeout 180

# AND THE SESSION IS vmuser's - PipeWire refuses root (`ConditionUser=!root`).
step "the console will say \"vmuser\""
  until vmuser
  from console
  timeout 180

# THE SESSION'S OWN PROCESS NAME, which only appears once it is running.
step "the console will say \"ARCH-SESSION-STARTING: deepin\""
  until "ARCH-SESSION-STARTING: deepin"
  from console
  timeout 180

step "wait 20s"
  settle 20

# TWENTY SECONDS AT A DESKTOP, so the capture is a machine that stayed up.
step "wait 20s"
  settle 20

# AND THE PIXELS, FROM THE DEVICE THE CONSOLE EXPORTS. `read:` is qemu's screendump of the
# framebuffer virtio-gpu put on the PCIe bus - the same surface EasyVM's noVNC shows. An
# X server that started but drew nothing, or that never took the VT, leaves a uniform frame
# and fails the checks below.
step "read the whole screen as \"screen\""
  read
    name screen

# TWO QUESTIONS ABOUT ONE FRAME, BECAUSE "NOT BLACK" HAS TWO FAILURE SHAPES. A guest with no
# device records a uniformly BLACK frame; a server that never drew records a uniformly
# COLOURED one, which is not black but is equally empty. MEASURED: a dead frame is mean 0.0
# with a mean deviation of 0.03, while the desktops here measure mean 2.6..134.
step "the screen is not black"
  check
    must true
    source screen
    mode mean_between
    name screen_is_not_black
    range [1, 255]
    rect [0, 0, 1024, 768]
    rect_at [1024, 768]

step "the screen is not one flat colour"
  check
    must true
    source screen
    mode spread_between
    name screen_has_content
    range [1, 128]
    rect [0, 0, 1024, 768]
    rect_at [1024, 768]

step "stop the machine by killing it, waiting up to 60s"
  stop kill
  timeout 60
